    debrief: "<p>A claim is a request for storage that outlives pods; the StorageClass turned it into a real volume the moment a pod needed it. notes now keeps its data across restarts (with <code>Recreate</code>, because only one node can hold a ReadWriteOnce volume), and PostgreSQL runs as a StatefulSet: <code>db-0</code> always comes back to <code>data-db-0</code>, even after being scaled away.</p><p>Deleting the claim deletes the data (reclaim policy <code>Delete</code>): back it up like any database.</p>",
